menu "Dongle bridge options"

config DONGLE_RADIO
	bool "Bluetooth LE radio to the wrist remotes"
	default n
	help
	  Selects src/radio_ble.c, the BLE central that talks
	  RADIO_PROTOCOL.md v1.0 to two wrist remotes.

	  n selects src/radio_null.c: both remotes report DISCONNECTED,
	  the downlink is rendered on the board's two LEDs, and the whole
	  wire layer runs unchanged, driven by the TEST modes.

	  THE n CONFIGURATION IS RETAINED PERMANENTLY. It is not scaffolding
	  and it is not a milestone that was green once. PLAN.md §3.10 lists
	  eight ways adding a radio degrades a working USB link without
	  touching any USB code, and every one of them is diagnosed by asking
	  whether it still happens with the radio compiled out. A baseline
	  you can re-run in thirty seconds answers that.

	  This defaults to n only because radio_ble.c does not exist yet; it
	  flips to y at Stage 3 (PLAN.md §3.1) when it does.

	  It REPLACES the deleted DONGLE_FAKE_LINK, which reported both
	  remotes CONNECTED with a fixed RSSI and battery. That symbol was
	  deleted rather than defaulted off: it fabricated exactly the values
	  a link test measures, and it did so plausibly, so a forgotten y
	  produced a passing test. A default is no protection when the
	  failure mode is forgetting.

config DONGLE_CONN_INTERVAL_UNITS
	int "BLE connection interval, in 1.25 ms units"
	depends on DONGLE_RADIO
	default 6
	range 6 3200
	help
	  6 units = 7.5 ms, rung 3 of RADIO_PROTOCOL.md §12.2 and the
	  baseline for the whole programme. It is a Kconfig value rather
	  than a header constant because it is the one tuning number with a
	  hardware consequence behind it: it feeds the power budget, and
	  through that the battery sizing and the PCB.

	  A later descent to 2.5 ms (SCI, rung 1) triples connection events
	  per second, so an undersized battery would become a respin. Size
	  with headroom. SCI is a deferred contingency, revisited only if
	  body shadowing proves a problem on custom hardware.

	  Both connections must use the identical interval — central
	  scheduling needs a common factor between them or their events
	  collide.

config DONGLE_SET_SERIAL_FALLBACK
	string "Officiating set serial used before provisioning exists"
	default "RR-0000"
	help
	  Reported in the fourth field of HELLO until the provisioning
	  record is read from flash (Stage 2), after which this is removed.

	  The default is deliberately not plausible. The app displays this
	  value for the referee's pre-match check against the label on the
	  hardware (PROTOCOL.md §4.1, FS §12.3), and a placeholder that
	  looked like a real serial would pass that check.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
